  "version": 2,
  "title": "From Code to AI Workflow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "f92bb232",
      "type": "text",
      "position": {
        "x": -736,
        "y": -104
      },
      "data": {
        "html": "<h1>Summary</h1><p></p><p>Our team wanted to <mark>accommodate increasing customer's needs in time series data anomaly detection (tsAD)</mark>. I helped the team to define the product scope, establish project lifecycle, and design and test the UI from scratch.</p><p></p><p>The MVP was adopted by <mark>600+ customers</mark>, quickly validating our initial direction. This may not be a big number in consumer section, but for a specialized domain, it was a strong signal that we were solving a real customer need.</p>",
        "size": "sm"
      },
      "width": 336,
      "height": 336
    },
    {
      "id": "8c694f61",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -800,
        "y": -176
      },
      "data": {
        "html": "<p>🫘 this is team work! I worked with 1 researcher and 5 engineers to build this app</p>",
        "color": "yellow",
        "size": "sm",
        "rotation": -10.2
      },
      "width": 128,
      "height": 112,
      "zIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "cc8f16e3",
      "type": "text",
      "position": {
        "x": -728,
        "y": 400
      },
      "data": {
        "html": "<h1>Background</h1><p></p><p>Industrial engineers need to identify anomalous patterns in physical-system data early to prevent equipment failures and reduce operational costs.</p><p></p><p>This need is growing: <mark>the global anomaly detection market is estimated at $7–8B in 2026</mark>, and our team had also received direct requests from our top customers.</p>",
        "size": "sm"
      },
      "width": 320,
      "height": 320
    },
